## Summary
The article introduces the Mundaneum, an early 20th-century project in Mons, Belgium, that aimed to compile and organize global knowledge on millions of index cards, serving as a precursor to modern internet technology. Visiting this historical site can fundamentally alter one's perception of everyday technology.

## Key Points
- The Mundaneum is an early concept resembling the internet for knowledge organization.
- It stored vast amounts of information on physical index cards, predating digital systems.
- Located in Mons, Belgium, it is now a museum or historical site.
- It highlights the evolution of information management and technology.
- Despite its dull-sounding name, it holds significant historical and technological value.


